1.1. Scope.  This License applies only to Enterprise Features. Software that Kepler makes available under an open-source license is governed by that license and not by this License, and nothing in this License limits any right you have under an open-source license to software distributed under it.
1.2. Acceptance.  By accessing, installing, copying, modifying, or otherwise using any Enterprise Feature, you accept this License. If you do not accept it, you must not use any Enterprise Feature. If you accept this License on behalf of an entity, you represent that you have authority to bind that entity, and you refers to that entity.
1.3. Relationship to a Written Agreement.  This License is the default and minimum set of terms on which Enterprise Features are made available. It is not intended to displace, and does not displace, terms you and Kepler have separately agreed in a signed writing. Where you and Kepler have entered into a master services agreement, terms of service, order form, Component Exhibit, or other executed agreement covering an Enterprise Feature (together, Your Agreement), Your Agreement governs that Enterprise Feature to the extent of any conflict with this License, and this License continues to apply to everything Your Agreement does not address. This License ranks below the applicable order form, below any Component Exhibit with respect to the license grant, scope and term for the Enterprise Feature that Component Exhibit covers, and below the master agreement, in each case in accordance with the order of precedence stated in Your Agreement. This License does not amend Your Agreement, and nothing in this License varies the intellectual-property, limitation-of-liability or indemnification provisions of Your Agreement.
1.4. Changes to This License.  Kepler may publish a revised version of this License. A revised version applies prospectively, from the date it is published, to Enterprise Features you first access under it. It does not apply retroactively to a paid subscription term already in effect under an executed order form, which continues to be governed by the version of this License in effect when that term began, unless you agree otherwise.

2. DEFINITIONS.
“Component Exhibit” means an exhibit to an order form between you and Kepler that identifies one or more Enterprise Features enabled for you and states any terms specific to them.

“Development and Testing” means running an Enterprise Feature locally or in a non-production environment for the purpose of evaluating it, developing it, developing against it, or testing it or modifications to it, in each case where the environment does not serve, support or process the data of your end users, customers or business operations.

“Enterprise Feature” means any component, module, feature, or functionality of the Mastra software that Kepler designates as an Enterprise Feature, including in the applicable source repository, in the software itself, in its documentation, or in a Component Exhibit. Enterprise Features are identified by designation and not by name in this License.

“License Key” means a credential issued by Kepler that enables one or more Enterprise Features and records the scope, permitted purpose, and expiry of that enablement.

“Production Use” means any use of an Enterprise Feature other than Development and Testing, including any use that serves, supports, or processes the data of your end users, customers or business operations.

